    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d548">

                <pb facs="0545" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/955</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-23T19:00:00-03:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 23, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 24, 1.55
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs wishes to prevent proposed Latin-American
                    congress, or, if this proves impossible, to <pb facs="0546" n="374"
                        xml:id="pg374"/> impose the condition that acceptance of invitation depends
                    upon? acceptance of principle that relations with Germany shall be broken. He
                    approves Peru’s attitude and is encouraging Bolivia to follow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
